    "done_when": "Make the kernel-backed topology read trace the Biot kernel once per stage instead of thirty times, with identical results, and measure what that buys. Measured by the derivative-rules probe (run r-20261006T015404732285, probes under its run directory): at 132 cells the read traces 1,373,538 expanded equations from 30 inlined kernel traces, 20 of BiotMomentCoupling.value_gradient (10 direct value calls in _point_values, the wall-event and curvature maps, and inside evaluate) and 10 of the jacfwd evaluate; one primal point kernel compiles cold on CPU in 23.5 s at 1.87 GB RSS, and one single-direction jvp of its field rows does not compile in 420 s. Done when: (1) in nova/equilibrium/topology.py every stage of read that evaluates the kernel at several points does so through one batched evaluation (one jax.vmap or one stacked call of value_gradient over all of that stage's points, and one jacfwd evaluate over the stage's stacked points), so the traced read contains at most one primal and one differentiated kernel trace per stage, and the census probe (reuse read_census.py from that run directory) reports the trace count and the expanded equation count before and after; (2) identity: on both analytic states at 132, 300 and 550 cells every TopologyRead field (nulls, values, gradients, Hessians, fractions, verdicts, reason codes) agrees with the base read to relative 1e-13 or exactly for integers, printed per field; (3) the existing tests/equilibrium/test_topology_read.py passes by delta against the base on the H200 lane, every strict expected failure still expected or unexpectedly passing only by qualification; (4) cold compile in fresh cache-disabled processes on the H200 for the read at 132, 300 and 550 cells and for the point kernel primal against its single-direction jvp, each bounded at 900 s, with wall, expanded equations, executable bytes and peak host RSS, in one job; (5) an evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/converged-forward-solve/cfs-read-shared-kernel.html (plan-evidence-for converged-forward-solve) with one table of those measurements, the job ids and the gate commands, reckon audit-doc 0 errors. Negative control: the read with one stage reverted to per-point kernel calls must show the trace count rising back, printed by the census probe. Gates run on compute, never the login node: H200 jobs through RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/h200_test_lane/run.sh --log (an absolute path under the run directory named in the manifest) --wait -- (the targets of that step); CPU measurements on all_debug with srun (TMPDIR=/tmp, JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu, the shared interpreter /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python run directly with PYTHONPATH set to the run worktree, orientation_worktree in the manifest, never uv on a compute node). Every cold compile runs in a fresh subprocess with the persistent compilation cache disabled in the environment before jax is imported, and asserts a cache miss from the guard rows. Any wait is declared with wait_probe sacct -n -X -P -j (job id) -o State and wait_terminal COMPLETED FAILED CANCELLED TIMEOUT OUT_OF_MEMORY NODE_FAIL, never exit:0. Every login-node uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync; configure_dtypes() before any array and jax_enable_x64 asserted True. Base-revision code is loaded through importlib from git show at the run orientation_base_sha under a different module name, never copied into the tree. No public signature changes. Figures, if any, go under docs/figures/kernel-derivative-rules. Commit with conventional subjects and bodies at every step and write the manifest before every job wait; the manifest commits line lists every commit.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
